description:
This dataset provides a comprehensive overview of school performance within the D75 district, featuring 24 unique schools categorized into three types: Elementary, Middle, and K-8. Each school is identified by a unique district borough number (dbn) and includes essential details such as the school name, principal, and enrollment figures, which range from 166 to 502 students. The dataset includes various performance metrics, including overall scores that span from 27.1 to 91.1, overall grades from A to F, and rankings from 1 to 9, reflecting the schools' performance in areas such as student progress, performance, and environment. This information can be utilized by educators, policymakers, and researchers to analyze school effectiveness, identify areas for improvement, and support decision-making processes aimed at enhancing educational outcomes. The dataset serves as a valuable resource for understanding the dynamics of school performance and addressing achievement gaps within the district.

Column constraints outlined in Data Dictionary:
dbn: required; format: string pattern (e.g., "75K036" where the first two characters are digits, followed by a letter and three digits)  
school_name: required; format: string  
school_type: allowed values: {Elementary, Middle, K-8}  
overall_score: value range: 0.0 to 100.0; required  
overall_grade: allowed values: {A, B, C, D, F}  
rank: value range: 1 to 9; required  
progress_grade: allowed values: {A, B, C, D, F}  
performance_grade: allowed values: {A, B, C, D, F}  
environment_grade: allowed values: {A, B, C, D, F}  
closing_the_achievement_gap: value range: 0.0 to 10.0; required  
principal: required; format: string  
enrollment: value range: 0 to 1000; required

This dataset provides detailed information on average class sizes across various educational programs in different boroughs, including Queens, Manhattan, Brooklyn, Bronx, and Staten Island. It categorizes data by grade level, program type, department, and subject, allowing for comprehensive analysis of educational structures. The dataset includes 451 unique values for the number of students, ranging from 8 to 36,035, and 257 unique values for the number of classes, with class sizes averaging between 5.3 and 35.1 students. It features various program types such as General Education, Integrated Co-Teaching, and Self-Contained classes, which cater to diverse learning needs. This dataset can be utilized to assess educational equity, analyze class size impacts on student learning, and inform policy decisions regarding resource allocation in schools. Overall, it serves as a valuable resource for educators, researchers, and policymakers interested in understanding and improving educational outcomes.

Column constraints outlined in Data Dictionary:
borough: allowed values are {Queens, Manhattan, Brooklyn, Bronx, Staten Is}  
grade_level: allowed values are {HS Core, MS Core}  
program_type: allowed values are {Gen Ed, ICT, G&T, SC, Acc}; required  
department: allowed values are {Math, Science, English, Social Studies}

This dataset provides a comprehensive overview of student suspensions across various schools, categorized by school year, demographic attributes, and administrative districts. It includes data on multiple demographic categories such as race, gender, age, and special education status, allowing for detailed analysis of suspension trends among different student groups. The dataset spans three school years and features 1755 unique school identifiers, ensuring a broad representation of educational institutions. Each entry includes the official school name and its location category, facilitating geographic analysis. The data can be utilized to assess the impact of suspensions on diverse student populations, identify patterns related to student demographics, and inform policy decisions aimed at reducing suspensions and promoting equitable educational environments. This dataset is particularly valuable for researchers, educators, and policymakers focused on understanding and addressing student behavior and disciplinary actions in schools.

Column constraints outlined in Data Dictionary:
report_category: allowed_values must be one of {Race, Gender, Grade Level, Age, ELL, SWD, STH}  
demographic_category: allowed_values must be one of {Race: American Indian/Alaskan Native, Asian, Black, Hispanic, White, Multi-Racial, Unknown, Total; Gender: Female, Male, Total; Grade Level: 0K, 1-12, Total; Age: 5-21, Total; ELL: NON-ELL, ELL, Total; SWD: Gen ED, SWD, Total; STH: NON-STH, STH, Total}  
dbn: format must be a string of 2 letters followed by 3 digits (e.g., XX000)
